diff --git a/.cartridge/docs/owner-attachment.md b/.cartridge/docs/owner-attachment.md
index b15d248..e77eeec 100644
--- a/.cartridge/docs/owner-attachment.md
+++ b/.cartridge/docs/owner-attachment.md
@@ -46,3 +46,44 @@ owner. Other attached readers remain usable. Remove `owner` to restore the
 existing local-owner behavior, including exclusive-writer refusal while another
 process owns that store. No persisted format, profile or daemon protocol changes
 are required.
+
+## Readiness without starting an engine
+
+Use `{"op":"status"}` for cached native readiness, or
+`{"op":"status","probe":true,"timeout_ms":2000}` for an explicit observation.
+The timeout is 1–60000 milliseconds; attached probes also respect the configured
+owner timeout. Other fields are rejected. Existing `ready` and `health` retain
+their previous responses and may initialize an engine in local-owner mode.
+
+Status always distinguishes `registered:true` from store, exact-ID read,
+semantic-query and model availability. `view`, `observation` and `age_ms` name
+whether the response came from a cache, an operation or a probe, and how old it
+is. Cached requests perform no filesystem, socket or model I/O. There is no
+background readiness polling.
+
+A local probe samples an existing regular writer lock without creating or
+rewriting it. A held lock reports `unavailable`, `writer_busy`, `retryable:true`.
+A missing/free lock reports `starting`, `local_uninitialized`; it does not prove
+a usable store or start an engine. Initialization and lock sampling exclude one
+another. An initialized engine supplies its existing graph-free readiness view.
+Attached probes verify store/PID identity and ask `ready` on that same transport.
+They never fall back to local ownership.
+
+A successful real semantic query by this caller establishes observed semantic
+readiness for 30 seconds on that owner PID. A recent failed semantic request with an available transport is
+`degraded`; transport failures are `unavailable` and clear semantic evidence.
+Older evidence or a successor PID is `unknown`. Exact-ID route
+readiness can be observed independently of embedding availability. Probing does
+not refresh the semantic evidence timestamp. The existing RPC query parser and
+filter validation exclude invalid requests from this evidence; registry-dependent
+claim-kind filters conservatively remain unobserved. Model availability stays `unknown`
+and `actively_probed:false`; exposed failure counters are historical observations.
+A recent successful query is not a promise that the next query will succeed.
+
+Only one status probe can run per service. Concurrent probes return
+`starting/probe_in_progress`, while cached requests remain responsive. A timed-out
+filesystem worker retains admission until it actually exits, so timeouts cannot
+launch an unbounded queue of blocking probes. Status does not claim to cancel a
+blocked filesystem syscall or work already running on an owner. Disposal retains
+its existing call-drain semantics. Responses contain static reasons and bounded
+counters, never credentials, paths, writer labels, query text or raw backend errors.
